<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Title 1"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{51C45913-886B-0E8B-28FF-19817136D4D7}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="title"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr><a:normAutofit fontScale="90000"/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Hybrid Control strategy for Modern MMC-based HVDC systems</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Text Placeholder 2"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{1E8204BD-011A-E2CC-799B-F668F3E01BBB}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="698500" y="1800520"/><a:ext cx="7927026" cy="4147844"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="00A6D6"/></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>Why? </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Grid short circuit ratio is becoming more unpredictable.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>To merge GFL and GFM advantages and make their demerits insignificant.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="00A6D6"/></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>How?</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Using the concept of </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" b="1" dirty="0"/><a:t>polytopic Lyapunov functions</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t> to define switching boundaries, which makes this control and the system inherently large signal stable.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="00A6D6"/></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>Applications?</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>To combat the sudden SCR variations in the AC grid connected to the HVDC network to ensure uninterrupted and stable power transmission.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>To mitigate faults and other unexpected transient phenomena by rapidly switching between GFL and GFM as and when required, as defined by the PLF polytopes.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="5" name="Content Placeholder 4" descr="A blue square with a black background&#xA;&#xA;AI-generated content may be incorrect."><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{FE07B4F5-44F9-F2AC-ACC9-E84179FE17F3}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId2" cstate="print"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{28A0092B-C50C-407E-A947-70E740481C1C}"><a14:useLocalDpi xmlns:a14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2010/main" val="0"/></a:ext></a:extLst></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill